    "created_at": "2016-09-08T14:09:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-08T14:09:11Z",
    "body": "> AFAICT in WebKit/Blink a later meta wins over the XML decl (not sure if it's because the parser changes the encoding or the prescan looks for both)\n\nPer the code it's because the prescan looks for both, kind of. The prescan algorithm is the one presented in #1752:\n- If byte-sniffing finds the document to start with UTF-16BE/LE `<?xm or UTF-32BE/LE`<?`, use that and skip further prescanning\n- Otherwise, if byte-sniffing finds the document to start with ASCII `<?xml`, use the naive XML encoding grabber to set an encoding for now, but also continue onward\n- Do the meta charset scanning\n\n(Note: as far as I can tell, this whole algorithm does not ignore leading whitespace. Maybe I missed it. I should test, if we do decide to go with that algorithm.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
